sentences.l:
but from him Apollo kept off
all unseemly treatment from the skin, pitying the man
even though he was dead;

Him now you have not endured, though he is a corpse, to save,
for his own wife to see, and his mother, and his own child,
and his father Priam, and the people,

But he, when he had taken his dear heart from heavenly Hector,
fastening him to the horses, round the tomb of his dear companion
drags him;
